[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2741191931","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104395#issuecomment-2741191931","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104395","id":2741191931,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6jY0T7","user":{"login":"derek-mcblane","id":11747622,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNzQ3NjIy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11747622?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/derek-mcblane","html_url":"https://github.com/derek-mcblane","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/derek-mcblane/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/derek-mcblane/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/derek-mcblane/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/derek-mcblane/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/derek-mcblane/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/derek-mcblane/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/derek-mcblane/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/derek-mcblane/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/derek-mcblane/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-20T17:29:07Z","updated_at":"2025-03-20T17:29:07Z","body":"I'll do my best to fill in the TODOs here in the next week or so.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2741191931/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2745943733","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104395#issuecomment-2745943733","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104395","id":2745943733,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6jq8a1","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-23T00:59:29Z","updated_at":"2025-03-23T01:00:12Z","body":"This is likely a consequence of https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100241 reworking ReflectionProbe blending.\n\nOut of curiosity, what were you using blending for (by adjusting intensity)? In my experience, most blending is based on the position of each probe, rather than intensity.\n\ncc @lander-vr ","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2745943733/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2745996280","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104395#issuecomment-2745996280","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104395","id":2745996280,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6jrJP4","user":{"login":"derek-mcblane","id":11747622,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNzQ3NjIy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11747622?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/derek-mcblane","html_url":"https://github.com/derek-mcblane","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/derek-mcblane/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/derek-mcblane/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/derek-mcblane/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/derek-mcblane/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/derek-mcblane/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/derek-mcblane/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/derek-mcblane/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/derek-mcblane/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/derek-mcblane/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-23T03:21:43Z","updated_at":"2025-03-23T03:39:58Z","body":"@Calinou, I think you're right.  That's kind of a bummer, I'll have to find another way to get this effect.\n\nI'm very new to Godot, so I don't know if there's a better way to do something like this or not.\n\nI made a MeshInstance3D for the \"light\" based on the Predator Arena light. Here's an IRL photo demonstrating the effect I'm going for https://www.reddit.com/media?url=https%3A%2F%2Fpreview.redd.it%2Fperimeter-billiard-light-review-v0-7g69mldi8xbc1.jpg%3Fwidth%3D3024%26format%3Dpjpg%26auto%3Dwebp%26s%3D2352da9e889efdaf01b2b132272ba7fcef2b4c8d\n\nThe reflection from the white texture was not very bright, even with intensity set to 1.\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/27d8cdeb-5cf2-4cc0-b6f5-5a609e75125d)\n\nSo I split the reflection probe into one for the light and one for the table.  Then I used a script to change the intensity to 10 for just the light, and got this much better result: ![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/cda28588-150f-4c53-9c97-e5ca2e774aec).\n(This also has some lighting and material tweaks, so it's not a perfect before/after).\n\nThe only thing I can think of that might affect this is that I'm using inches as my distance unit.  So effectively everything is scaled up ~40x.  That means light intensities need to be much higher.  This isn't actually a light, though, so I wouldn't expect that to have any impact.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2745996280/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2754177721","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104395#issuecomment-2754177721","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104395","id":2754177721,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6kKWq5","user":{"login":"lander-vr","id":31851431,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxODUxNDMx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/31851431?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr","html_url":"https://github.com/lander-vr","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-26T12:04:39Z","updated_at":"2025-03-26T12:04:39Z","body":"> Out of curiosity, what were you using blending for (by adjusting intensity)? In my experience, most blending is based on the position of each probe, rather than intensity.\n\nThis is correct, intensity doesn't have any effect on blending. Blending is based on a combination of position, the AABB extents, and the new blend distance property.\n\n\n> The reflection from the white texture was not very bright, even with intensity set to 1.\n\nI'm curious why you cannot increase the emissive intensity of the texture itself, instead of increasing the intensity of the reflection probe:\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e4cf9332-109d-4e97-815c-32d0560750d9)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2754177721/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2755406846","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104395#issuecomment-2755406846","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104395","id":2755406846,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6kPCv-","user":{"login":"derek-mcblane","id":11747622,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNzQ3NjIy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11747622?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/derek-mcblane","html_url":"https://github.com/derek-mcblane","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/derek-mcblane/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/derek-mcblane/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/derek-mcblane/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/derek-mcblane/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/derek-mcblane/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/derek-mcblane/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/derek-mcblane/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/derek-mcblane/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/derek-mcblane/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-26T18:30:34Z","updated_at":"2025-03-26T18:30:49Z","body":"@lander-vr, I think I tried increasing the emissive intensity, but it didn’t work. Maybe it’s a difference between Mobile and Forward+. Or maybe it’s the length scaling I mentioned.\n\nI’ll play around with this again, thanks for the suggestion.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2755406846/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2755421298","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104395#issuecomment-2755421298","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104395","id":2755421298,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6kPGRy","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-26T18:37:00Z","updated_at":"2025-03-26T18:37:11Z","body":">  I think I tried increasing the emissive intensity, but it didn’t work. Maybe it’s a difference between Mobile and Forward+. Or maybe it’s the length scaling I mentioned.\n\nMobile has more limited dynamic range (it can't go above `2.0`, i.e. twice as bright as standard white), which applies to the ReflectionProbe's cubemaps too.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2755421298/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2755433396","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104395#issuecomment-2755433396","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104395","id":2755433396,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6kPJO0","user":{"login":"derek-mcblane","id":11747622,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNzQ3NjIy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11747622?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/derek-mcblane","html_url":"https://github.com/derek-mcblane","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/derek-mcblane/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/derek-mcblane/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/derek-mcblane/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/derek-mcblane/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/derek-mcblane/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/derek-mcblane/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/derek-mcblane/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/derek-mcblane/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/derek-mcblane/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-26T18:42:30Z","updated_at":"2025-03-26T18:42:30Z","body":"Okay got it. Any suggestions on how to get this effect with the Mobile renderer?","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2755433396/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2760991133","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104395#issuecomment-2760991133","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104395","id":2760991133,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6kkWGd","user":{"login":"lander-vr","id":31851431,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxODUxNDMx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/31851431?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr","html_url":"https://github.com/lander-vr","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-28T10:55:57Z","updated_at":"2025-03-28T10:55:57Z","body":"It's a little hacky maybe, but what you could do is darken all the lighting in your scene, but keep the emissive strength of that light shape material at `2.0` (or higher), then in the WorldEnvironment you could increase the exposure with `CameraAttributesPractical`.\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/edf8e1f9-abab-4061-a905-d134605efa1c)\n\nWe're essentially brightening up that light shape by increasing the exposure, but to keep the scene lighting the same we need to dim the light sources in the scene to compensate. :)\n\nIt does seem like there's an issue with reflection probes on mobile when using non standard exposure. After changing the exposure and then updating the refprobe capture, I get this: \n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f8746df6-87c1-4bc8-82bf-9d832e86a736)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2760991133/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2763386127","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104395#issuecomment-2763386127","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104395","id":2763386127,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6kte0P","user":{"login":"derek-mcblane","id":11747622,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNzQ3NjIy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11747622?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/derek-mcblane","html_url":"https://github.com/derek-mcblane","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/derek-mcblane/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/derek-mcblane/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/derek-mcblane/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/derek-mcblane/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/derek-mcblane/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/derek-mcblane/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/derek-mcblane/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/derek-mcblane/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/derek-mcblane/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-29T14:16:37Z","updated_at":"2025-03-29T14:16:37Z","body":"Makes sense, thanks for such a clear explanation! I think I actually tried something like this by changing tonemapping exposure settings and adjusting light intensities.\n\n> After changing the exposure and then updating the refprobe capture, I get this: ![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f8746df6-87c1-4bc8-82bf-9d832e86a736)\n\nI remember getting a result like this. Interesting that you say it’s an issue. Anything I can do to collect more information on this? Maybe a new bug should be opened.\n\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2763386127/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2763500716","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104395#issuecomment-2763500716","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104395","id":2763500716,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6kt6ys","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/s